 "module": "number-series",
 "intro": [
  "A number series hides one rule. Find it with a short list of tests, always in the same order: **gaps, gaps of gaps, ratios, multiply-and-add, taking turns**.",
  "There are eight short lessons: one per rule family, then the two question forms (wrong number, blank inside). Go in order the first time.",
  "What the papers ask (Stage A count in Quick revision: 70 IBPS Clerk questions from 15 papers, and about 24 in 7 sister papers, all memory-based):",
  "| Rule | Label | Lesson |",
  "| Gaps steady or growing evenly (NS1) | Confirmed, 11 Clerk papers | NS1 (two lessons) |",
  "| Gaps that are squares, cubes, primes, doubling (NS2) | Confirmed, 9 Clerk papers | NS2 |",
  "| Multiply or divide by changing numbers (NS4) | Confirmed, 11 Clerk papers | NS4 |",
  "| Multiply, then add (NS3) | Confirmed, 8 Clerk papers | NS3 |",
  "| Two patterns taking turns (NS6) | Confirmed, 8 Clerk papers | NS6 |"
 ],
 "needs": [],
 "after": [
  "That is the whole topic. The **Quick revision** tab has the tests in order and the drills.",
  "Speed comes from the first glance: slow growth means gaps; fast growth means ratios."
 ],
